WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.040
To celebrate the release of Avengers: Age
Of Ultron, let’s take a look at 12 things

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:11.460
you probably didn’t know about the second
Avengers team-up in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.700
There are five different versions of Captain
America’s shield which are used for filming.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.420
Chris Evans, who plays Captain America, prefers
to use the lightest version of the shield,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.289
which is made of biscuit foam, so it doesn’t
interfere with his acting.

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:29.070
However, that particular shield isn’t very
durable unlike the soft rubber shield which

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.480
is more hard-wearing but heavier.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:37.760
Andy Serkis was cast as arms dealer Ulysses
Klaw after the movie’s executive producer

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.379
Jeremy Latcham saw a fan’s mock-up of Serkis
as Klaue online!

00:00:43.379 --> 00:00:48.420
To bring the Hulk and Ultron to life, Mark
Ruffalo and James Spader worked closely with

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.219
Andy Serkis’s performance capture company,
The Imaginarium Studios.

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:57.359
So that Ruffalo had a real sense of the Hulk’s
size, weights and inhibitors were put on his

00:00:57.359 --> 00:00:58.359
body.

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:03.660
And to create the Hulk’s roar on set, they
used a sound system and pitch-modulated Ruffalo’s

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.660
voice.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.390
According to Ruffalo, the technology for capturing
the Hulk’s performance had improved since

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:13.170
filming The Avengers, so this time they could
capture his facial and body movements at the

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:18.930
same time, instead of separately, which really
helped him bring the Hulk to life.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.850
To bring Scarlet Witch’s powers to the big
screen, writer-director Joss Whedon was not

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.430
only inspired by images from the comic books,
but also by how dancers move.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:33.570
So, Elizabeth Olsen, who plays Scarlet Witch,
worked with dancer and movement coach Jenny

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.490
White to create fluid hand and arm movements
to bring her character’s powers to visual

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.050
life on screen and really get her physicality
right.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:48.270
Black Widow’s new fighting batons were inspired
by Escrima Sticks, which are used in traditional

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.990
Filipino Martial Arts.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:54.680
However, unlike traditional Escrima Sticks,
Black Widow’s batons are charged so she

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.812
can deliver a jolt of power when she hits
an opponent.

00:01:56.812 --> 00:02:04.340
The search for Baron von Strucker’s stronghold
began a year before production started.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:08.950
The filmmakers wanted an impressive-looking
building with a cinematic setting in a region

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:14.650
little seen on screen, so the location scouts
spent two months visiting potential historical

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:15.980
sites in Europe.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:21.840
In the end, Fort Bard, a 19th-century fortified
complex in north-west Italy’s Aosta Valley,

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.070
was used as Strucker’s Hydra Research Base
in the fictional Eastern European setting

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.690
of Sokovia.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:33.040
The Hulkbuster sequence was filmed over two
weeks in the Central Business District of

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.880
Johannesburg in South Africa.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:40.000
The shoot involved flying helicopters, crashing
cars and exploding huge pyrotechnics in the

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.000
city.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.920
Black Widow’s vision was filmed at Tring
Park School For The Performing Arts, which

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.810
is located in Hertfordshire, England, and
specialises in dance.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:54.310
The scenes featured a number of the school’s
ballet students practising in its dance studio.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:59.200
Former pupils of the school include Star Wars:
The Force Awakens star Daisy Ridley and Downton

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.860
Abbey actress Jessica Brown Findlay.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.490
Although the Avengers Tower is located in
New York City, the massive set for the Tower’s

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:12.280
interior was created by the movie’s production
designer Charles Wood at Shepperton Studios

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.830
in the UK.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:18.300
Scenes in the Tower feature heavily in the
film so, to give Joss Whedon plenty of variety

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.920
for filming, Wood and his team designed a
huge set with different interconnected levels

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.471
and multiple areas including laboratories,
lounges, and locker rooms.

00:03:26.471 --> 00:03:32.970
In fact, the Avengers Tower is the biggest
set built for a Marvel movie so far.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.810
To film Captain America’s chase scene with
a speeding truck, Seoul’s Mapo Bridge, which

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:42.530
is a large multi-lane two-way bridge that
crosses the Han River in South Korea, was

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.520
shut down completely.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:48.410
Prior to shooting the sequence on the bridge,
the movie’s crew rehearsed the stunts needed

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.930
on an unopened motorway nearby.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:57.820
The Avengers’ Quinjet was redesigned to
give it a more militaristic appearance, including

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.330
a pared-down, more functional-looking interior.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:05.900
As for the Quinjet’s canopy, that was inspired
by the look of helicopter cockpits, so it

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:12.130
has glass both in front and below, which gives
a real sense of speed when it’s flying.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:16.820
The movie’s epic final battle scene was
shot on location in both Italy’s Aosta Valley

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.820
region and in London, England!

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:23.700
Hendon Police College, which is the main training
centre for London’s Metropolitan Police,

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.450
was used for filming as it had an outdoor
space big enough to double as war-torn Sokovia

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:32.820
and accommodate the whole production for three
weeks as well as being secure from the prying

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.150
camera lenses of the paparazzi.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:38.970
The movie’s production designer built a
church on the site and the filmmakers used

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.050
drones to capture multiple angles during the
shoot.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:46.130
Director Joss Whedon has said that filming
in that church was “some of the best visceral

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.550
comic book stuff” he’s ever shot.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:53.030
Well there you have it, 12 things you probably
didn't know about Avengers: Age Of Ultron!

